@startuml use-case
' Nodebook use-case diagram (D3, issue #8).
' Requirement IDs (H1-H6) follow the project specification; see docs/diagrams/README.md.

title Nodebook · Use-case diagram
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #F7F9FC
  BorderColor #4A6FA5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBEA
  BorderColor #C9B458
}

actor "Visitor" as Visitor
actor "Registered user" as User
actor "LLM provider" as LLM <<external system>>

rectangle "Nodebook" {
  ' H1: accounts
  usecase "Register\n(H1)" as UC_Register
  usecase "Log in\n(H1)" as UC_Login
  usecase "Log out\n(H1)" as UC_Logout

  ' H2: notes
  usecase "Browse daily notes\n(H2)" as UC_Browse
  usecase "Create note\n(H2)" as UC_Create
  usecase "Edit note\n(H2)" as UC_Edit
  usecase "Delete note\n(H2)" as UC_Delete
  usecase "Open note\n(H2, H5, H6)" as UC_Open

  ' H3/H4: link suggestions
  usecase "Generate link suggestions\n(H3)" as UC_Suggest
  usecase "Review link suggestions\n(H4)" as UC_Review
  usecase "Accept link\n(H4)" as UC_Accept
  usecase "Reject link\n(H4)" as UC_Reject

  ' H5: graph
  usecase "Explore knowledge graph\n(H5)" as UC_Graph

  ' H6: question answering
  usecase "Ask a question\n(H6)" as UC_Ask

  ' Privacy (non-functional requirement)
  usecase "Export all data\n(privacy)" as UC_Export
  usecase "Delete account\n(privacy)" as UC_DeleteAccount
}

Visitor --> UC_Register
Visitor --> UC_Login

User --> UC_Logout
User --> UC_Browse
User --> UC_Create
User --> UC_Edit
User --> UC_Delete
User --> UC_Review
User --> UC_Graph
User --> UC_Ask
User --> UC_Export
User --> UC_DeleteAccount

UC_Create ..> UC_Suggest : <<include>>
UC_Edit ..> UC_Suggest : <<include>>
' Written base-first so extensions are laid out to the right of the use case they extend.
UC_Review <.. UC_Accept : <<extend>>
UC_Review <.. UC_Reject : <<extend>>
UC_Browse <.. UC_Open : <<extend>>
UC_Graph <.. UC_Open : <<extend>>
UC_Ask <.. UC_Open : <<extend>>

UC_Suggest --> LLM
UC_Ask --> LLM

note right of UC_Suggest
  Runs in the background after a save.
  Proposes up to 5 links, each with a score
  and a one-line reason. Only the user's own
  notes are candidates. An LLM failure never
  blocks saving the note; the job is retried.
end note

note right of UC_Ask
  The answer cites the notes it used.
  If no relevant note exists, the agent
  says so rather than answering from
  general knowledge.
end note

note bottom of UC_Login
  Every use case of the registered
  user requires being logged in.
end note

@enduml
